we all know that the products we manage  at some point must turn a profit so  whether you're working at a large  corporation with many products to manage  or churning away at a young startup  still searching for product market fit  everyone working in products  needs to have a basic knowledge of the  financial and cost accounting measures  that lead to profit  i'm mike levink professor of civil and  environmental engineering at stanford  and in this class i will show you how to  use the concepts of accounting and cost  management to make decisions and drive  product profitability  how to leverage the tools of accounting  and cost management to set product  targets and measure performance  and how to build upon the ideas of  accounting and cost management to plan  for product success and deliver value  don't worry i won't ask you to be a cpa  or to do any overly advanced math  but what i will show you is how to use  things like balance sheets income  statements and other financial documents  to make better product focused decisions  how to think more critically about  product pricing and cost and then manage  for product profit  and how to create product focus targets  and goals that align with your customers  your team and your company  i look forward to seeing you there
 

